{
  /*
   * Every App test file, as one program. `npm run compile` type-checks the
   * App's sources with ./tsconfig.json, which leaves Tests out, and then
   * these tests in parts that extend this file and change only what they
   * include (tsconfig.tests.dashboard.json, tsconfig.tests.featureset.json
   * and tsconfig.tests.rest.json): sources and tests as one program outgrew
   * the compile's 8 GiB heap on 2026-11-15 (#8503). scripts/compile-tests.js
   * explains the split, and checks that the parts leave no file of this one
   * out.
   *
   * The App's jest config transpiles only (ts-jest isolatedModules), so
   * nothing else type-checks a test. Everything but what is included is
   * inherited, so a test is held to the same rules as the code it tests.
   * The App's global declaration files are listed as well: the build picks
   * them up through its default include, and a test program would otherwise
   * only see what the tests import.
   *
   * Editors and ESLint's typed linting (projectService in eslint.config.js)
   * give each file the nearest tsconfig.json that includes it, so the parts
   * have one each: Tests/Dashboard, Tests/FeatureSet and Tests (the rest).
   */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["Tests/**/*.ts", "Tests/**/*.tsx", "Typings/**/*.d.ts"],
  // Not ./tsconfig.json's, which leaves Tests out.
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "build"]
}
